{"name":"Flesh and Blood","hex":"#cf3f4f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flesh and blood","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Consisting of flesh, blood, and other substances associated with animals or humans.","Real; substantial."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A human body; a person generally.","One's family, or member of one's family."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flesh_and_blood"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flesh and Blood (card game)","blocks":[{"text":"Flesh and Blood is a trading card game published by Legend Story Studios (LSS), an independent design studio based in Auckland, New Zealand. Gameplay focuses on two players who each control a single hero who battle one versus one to the death. It was designed by James White, who had previously played Magic: The Gathering professionally. The game is based on elements of fantasy and, to some extent, science fiction. The name of the game is meant to imply that the game was designed to be played in person instead of as an online game."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ed/Flesh_and_Blood_TCG_Logo.png/330px-Flesh_and_Blood_TCG_Logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flesh_and_Blood_(card_game)","wikidata":"Q109657155"},{"title":"Eucharist","blocks":[{"text":"The Eucharist, also called Holy Communion, the Blessed Sacrament or the Lord's Supper, is a Christian rite, considered a sacrament in most churches and an ordinance in others. Christians believe that the rite was instituted by Jesus Christ at the Last Supper, the night before his crucifixion, giving his disciples bread and wine. Passages in the New Testament state that he commanded them to \"do this in memory of me\" while referring to the bread as \"my body\" and the cup of wine as \"the blood of my covenant, which is poured out for many\". According to the synoptic Gospels, this was at a Passover meal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/St_Michael_the_Archangel%2C_Findlay%2C_OH_-_bread_and_wine_crop_1.jpg/330px-St_Michael_the_Archangel%2C_Findlay%2C_OH_-_bread_and_wine_crop_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eucharist","wikidata":"Q66086"},{"title":"Flesh and Blood (1985 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Flesh and Blood is a 1985 erotic historical adventure film directed by Paul Verhoeven, and starring Rutger Hauer, Jennifer Jason Leigh, Tom Burlinson, Susan Tyrrell, Ronald Lacey, Bruno Kirby and Jack Thompson. The script was written by Verhoeven and Gerard Soeteman. The story is set in 1501 in early modern Italy, and follows two warring groups of mercenaries and their longstanding quarrel."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0d/Poster_Flesh_%26_Blood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flesh_and_Blood_(1985_film)","wikidata":"Q1428124"},{"title":"Flesh","blocks":[{"text":"Flesh is any aggregation of soft tissues of an organism. Various multicellular organisms have soft tissues that may be called \"flesh\". In mammals, including humans, flesh encompasses muscles, fats and other loose connective tissues, but sometimes excludes non-muscular organs and typically discarded parts. More generally, it may be considered the portions of the body that are soft and delicate. In a culinary context, consumable animal flesh is called meat, while processed visceral tissues are known as offal."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flesh","wikidata":"Q13119823"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7a/Flesh_and_Blood_CCG_card_back.png/250px-Flesh_and_Blood_CCG_card_back.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7a/Flesh_and_Blood_CCG_card_back.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7a/Flesh_and_Blood_CCG_card_back.png/250px-Flesh_and_Blood_CCG_card_back.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlesh_and_Blood_CCG_card_back.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Flesh_and_Blood_Super_Slam_World_Premiere_Montreal_2025-09-14.jpg/500px-Flesh_and_Blood_Super_Slam_World_Premiere_Montreal_2025-09-14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Flesh_and_Blood_Super_Slam_World_Premiere_Montreal_2025-09-14.jpg/1280px-Flesh_and_Blood_Super_Slam_World_Premiere_Montreal_2025-09-14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Flesh_and_Blood_Super_Slam_World_Premiere_Montreal_2025-09-14.jpg/500px-Flesh_and_Blood_Super_Slam_World_Premiere_Montreal_2025-09-14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flesh and Blood Super Slam World Premiere at the Palais des Congrès de Montréal on 14 September 2025.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlesh_and_Blood_Super_Slam_World_Premiere_Montreal_2025-09-14.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Flesh_and_Blood_card_game_2022.jpg/500px-Flesh_and_Blood_card_game_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Flesh_and_Blood_card_game_2022.jpg/1280px-Flesh_and_Blood_card_game_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Flesh_and_Blood_card_game_2022.jpg/500px-Flesh_and_Blood_card_game_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&u